Alright, I've been iteratively tweaking the logo animation HTML/CSS to improve its visual flow and reduce any jarring effects. So far, I've adjusted the fill animation timing, added a stroke-out keyframe, refined the sweep delay variable, and cleaned up some redundant opacity rules. The recent changes introduced a new keyframe `aiLogoStrokeOut202606` and tweaked the fill source animation to use a smoother cubic-bezier curve and a longer duration. I also ensured the fill stays transparent during the draw phase.

Now I need to look at the JavaScript (or inline script) that handles the fill source elements. Earlier in the file, there was a block that iterated over `candidates` (presumably SVG path elements) and did two things:
1. Added the class `ai-fill-source-202606` to each element.
2. Forced the fill style to `'transparent'` manually to prevent white blocks from flashing before the animation starts.

Given the recent CSS changes, the class `ai-fill-source-202606` already sets `opacity:0` and later animates to opacity 1. Forcing `el.style.fill = 'transparent'` is redundant and potentially conflicts with the intended fill behavior, especially now that the fill is supposed to fade in with the animation rather than be forced transparent via inline style. Moreover, the comment I added earlier mentions that the fill should stay transparent during the draw, but the CSS already handles that with `fill:transparent!important;` on the appropriate selectors. Keeping the inline style may also make it harder to override later if the animation wants to change the fill color.

Therefore, I should simplify this code block: remove the explicit `el.style.fill = 'transparent'` line, and add a comment explaining the logic—namely that the original fills remain on the elements, but the `ai-fill-source-202606` class will hide them via opacity until the draw completes, after which they fade in. Also, I can condense the `forEach` to a single line for clarity.

The exact string to replace is the old block:
```
      candidates.forEach(el => {
        el.classList.add('ai-fill-source-202606');
        // Force fill to transparent so we don't see white blocks before animation starts
        el.style.fill = 'transparent'; 
      });
```
I will replace it with:
```
// Original fills stay on the elements; the fill-source class hides them
// via opacity until the draw completes, then fades them in.
candidates.forEach(el => el.classList.add('ai-fill-source-202606'));
```
This aligns with the updated CSS approach and removes unnecessary inline styling. I’ll use the Edit tool with `replace_all: false` to make this precise substitution in `/home/lane/log/logo.html`.

